$ Small exact-XNL reference, deep-water transfer with WAM depth scaling (QUADRUPLET 52)
$
$ SWINTFXNL maps IQUAD 51, 52 and 53 onto its own iq_quad by subtracting 50,
$ so the three are separate transfer routines. Only 51 had a deck; 52 and 53
$ were declared formulations that no input ever selected. They run over 15 m
$ depth -- the 0.3 factor on the same bathymetry file -- rather than the 50 m
$ of quad_xnl.swn, because depth scaling and the finite-depth transfer have
$ nothing to do at deep-water depths.
PROJECT 'QUADXN52' '001'
SET CARTESIAN
MODE STATIONARY ONEDIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN

CGRID REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 100000.0 0.0 40 0 &
      CIRCLE 36 0.04 1.0 34
INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 1 0 100000.0 1.0
READINP BOTTOM 0.3 'bottom.bot' 1 0 FREE

WIND 15.0 0.0
BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 PEAK DSPR DEGREES
BOUNDSPEC SIDE WEST CONSTANT PAR 0.05 2.0 0.0 20.0

GEN3 WESTH
QUADRUPLET 52
OFF BREAKING

POINTS 'GAUGES' 0.0 0.0 25000.0 0.0 50000.0 0.0 &
         75000.0 0.0 100000.0 0.0
TABLE 'GAUGES' HEADER 'quad_xnl52.tbl' XP DEPTH HSIGN TM01 RTP REDTRIAD REDQUAD
SPECOUT 'GAUGES' SPEC1D ABS 'quad_xnl52.spc'
TEST 1 0 POINTS XY 50000.0 0.0 S1D 'quad_xnl52_sources.spc'

COMPUTE
STOP
